{
  "_doc": "Per-fixture DOT node-size ratchet for the description DOT-parity suite (mission S1L). Same convention as oracle/goldens/state|object/size-backlog.json: structurally EQUAL fixtures whose maxSizeDeltaIn (inches, max across their svek-N graphs) exceeds the 0.01in conformant bar; the test asserts delta <= pinned + 1e-6 per fixture, so pins only shrink. A sub-mission that makes a fixture conformant drops its delta to <=0.01 and DELETES the entry (absent slug => conformant required). Re-baselined 2026-07-27 after S1L-b (description [ ... ] display-body expansion) from scripts/measure-description-size-deltas.ts. 115 entries / 351 goldens => 236 (67.2%) conformant. S1L-b flipped dexigu-24/kenece-24/zifaji-87 (the HR-body trio) plus butebe-90/zavitu-69 to conformant (deleted). fariba-82 is pinned 1.024479: S1L-b T6 diagnosed it as a compound residual (out-of-scope awslib sprite + a jar `file`-body word-wrap gap, S1L-d), NOT a leaf-width bug -- see plans/s1l-leaf-sizing/ledger.md. zotiru-33 shrank 2.655 -> 0.914 (S1L-b T5 wired scoped `<style> package { MinimumWidth }`; the `not_nested` package is now exact at 4.583in, residual is the nested package cluster (S1L-e) + an unclosed-`<color>` note tag). Root-cause families + sub-mission routing are in plans/s1l-leaf-sizing/ledger.md. The 2 latex fixtures are a permanent inherent-tolerance DIVERGENCE (KaTeX != JLaTeXMath, see DIVERGENCES.md), excluded from the conformant denominator but still pinned here shrink-only. S1L-b-unicode (2026-07-27) landed the codepoint decode-ordering fix (<U+..>/&#..; decode per-line at measure time, AFTER the newline split): heights no longer over-split, so gafico-37 shrank 5.680208->3.752777 and nujito-06 3.350521->3.122049 (shrink-only). Still 236/351 (67.2%) conformant -- the 3 targets remain named width residuals, NOT emoji-width bugs: gafico-37 + nujito-06 are driven by the UNPORTED <code> creole block (node c, deferred E2r L2; tracked GH #24); lurupu-11 (2.045912, unchanged) by a sizer<->renderer creole-lexer divergence (parseCreole leaves unclosed <b>/<font Name> literal, buildStripeAtoms strips them). See ledger.md S1L-b-unicode T1/T2/T3. creole-lexer-unification (2026-07-27) unified the sizer+renderer creole lexers onto one shared StripeSimple.buildLineAtoms helper (sizer dropped parseCreole), and \u2014 scope-expanded \u2014 ported AtomImg's URL cannot-decode text faithfully (creole-atoms.ts cannotDecodeText: http/https raster -> '(Cannot decode: <url>)', .svg url -> '(Cannot decode SVG: <url>)') and fixed a pre-existing description-parser leak of the '[body] as alias' wrapper into node.display for the keyword+bracket form (component-table-containers KEYWORD_RE -> parseBracketDeclaration). Net: lurupu-11 (2.045912->conformant, the original target), pebace-74 (0.172570->conformant, bracket+URL), zotiru-33 (0.914108->conformant) DELETED; nobiza-91 1.460330->0.669271, tuliba-37 6.735899->0.521007, gevozu-46/sunuju-01 4.670->0.611632, vivido-49 2.519868->0.157407, jecici-56 3.182521->0.315278, xufexu-38 1.457690->0.152778, nenedo-78 0.864816->0.168803 all shrank (zero widened). gafico-37/nujito-06 stay pinned unchanged: the T1 spike DISPROVED the brief's premise that the lexer switch would shrink them (their <color>/<u> tags sit adjacent to a decoded <U+000A> where both lexers agree); their residual is the deferred node-c <code> block. Remaining nobiza-91 0.669271 residual = note cannot-decode text measured at NOTE font 13 vs the jar's 14 (separate pre-existing gap; tracked GH #23). Now 112 entries / 351 => 239 (68.1%) conformant. S1L-c (2026-07-28) ported the interface `hideText` leaf dimension: EntityImageDescription.java:137 sets `hideText = symbol == USymbols.INTERFACE` and :209-211 then builds `asSmall` from EMPTY name/desc/stereo, so an interface/circle leaf measures the bare CircleInterface2 square (radius 8 + margin 1 = 18px = 0.25in) regardless of its label -- the label is drawn OUTSIDE the node, and when the shield is not suppressed `getShield` reserves room for it as HTML-table margins rather than by growing the node. Our port had been sizing these as generic text boxes (leaf-sizing.ts#measureLeafNode, new INTERFACE_CIRCLE_SIZE case). That fix UNMASKED a separate pre-existing parser gap that it also closes: a bare quoted `\"Display\" as Alias` line (no type keyword) is CommandCreateElementFull's DISPLAY2/CODE2 branch with SYMBOL omitted, which java:272-275 resolves to actorStyle().toUSymbol() -- an ACTOR, which then makes DescriptionDiagram.isUsecase() true so every remaining STILL_UNKNOWN leaf mutes to actor too. RE_BARE_QUOTED_DECL only admitted the no-alias form, so xacaxe-43-bupe002's five leaves fell to interface and WIDENED 0.555556 -> 1.295833 under the sizing fix; with the `as` clause added they are all exact. Net: 239 -> 272 / 351 (68.1 -> 77.5 pct) conformant, zero widened, 33 entries DELETED, 2 shrank (cukafa-49 0.361111->0.305556, zosuje-43 0.222222->0.146702). The interface-shield bucket is now EMPTY. Two fixtures that bucket carried were misattributions, both corrected in scripts/measure-description-size-deltas.ts CAUSE_PATTERNS: turasu-73-zoni468 is a SPRITE fixture (the sprite regex lacked '/', so every stdlib '<$bundle/name>' fell through to the interface catch) -> S1L-f; cukafa-49-fona812 + gogamo-72-pibo470 are a per-element FONT skinparam gap ('skinparam componentFontSize 18' never reaches measureLeafNode -- fontSpec is one diagram-wide value, with no per-USymbol resolution) -> new S1L-h. Now 79 entries / 351 => 272 (77.5 pct) conformant. S1L-f part 1 (2026-07-28) -- ENGINE MISROUTING, not sprite sizing. `skinparam <selector><<stereo>> {` failed BOTH block-open regexes and fell through to RE_SKINPARAM_LINE, which read the key as `rectangle<<stereo>>` and the VALUE as `{`: the opener was consumed, no block opened, and the body LEAKED into the diagram as content. Every awslib/tupadr3 sprite include ends in an `AWSEntityColoring(x)`-style `!definelong` expanding to exactly that block, so kofuca-08-pafi749 accumulated 53 orphan `BackgroundColor`/`BorderColor`/`}` lines ahead of its real content -- burying the element declarations past descriptive-keywords.ts's SCAN_LINE_LIMIT, so hasDescriptiveElement returned false and dispatcher.ts#resolve fell back to the block's detected type, handing an AWS deployment diagram to the CLASS engine, which measured each node's raw `<img data:image/png;base64,...>` markup as label text (19214px vs the jar's 142px). Fixed in preprocessor.ts (scoped selector-block regex + stereotype appended AFTER the entry name, matching upstream's `param.name() + suffix + stereotype` concatenation). kofuca-08 478.939757 -> 0.305903 (1566x); its residual, and all of ruziru-69-xixo434 / bootstrap-0 (0.682747, correctly routed, ellipse shapes matching), is now GENUINE sprite-dimension resolution -- bundle sprites (`<$bi-globe>`, `,scale=2.5`) contribute no dims (node b measures 23.5x20 vs the jar's 69.5x56.8). That is the remaining S1L-f core. S1L-a (2026-07-28) ported the folder-family leaf: `folder` and `package` are ONE class, USymbolFolder(sname, showTitle) (USymbols.java:79/86), whose asSmall dimension is getMargin().addDimension(dimName.mergeTB(dimStereo, dimLabel)) with getMargin() = [30, 23] and dimName = showTitle ? title.calculateDimension() : FIXED XDimension2D(40, 15). mergeTB takes the MAX width and the SUM of heights, so for `folder` the fixed tab FLOORS the width as well as adding 15 to the height -- a floor this port lacked entirely (`folder b` measured 37.79 vs the jar's 70.00 = max(40, 7.79) + 30; it only bites on a SHORT name, which is why no fixture caught it). For `package` the title is the element CODE and the label carries the display only when the two differ, and the shown title contributes a measured +12px (FOLDER_SHOWN_TITLE_EXTRA_WIDTH -- exact at three widths, deltas 11.999996/11.999976/12.000008; NOT attributable to a single upstream expression, see the constant's own doc). Verified against the jar on all five forms: `package \"a b c d e f g\"` 91.787x37, `package pp as \"Display Here\"` 106.387x51, `package \"Disp Two\" as dd` 84.600x51, `folder \"x\"` 70.000x52, `folder ff as \"Folder Display\"` 115.750x52 -- all exact. 272 -> 279/351 (77.5 -> 79.5 pct), zero widened. NOTE: measureFolderLeaf must keep applying opts.minimumWidth -- omitting it regressed zotiru-33-legi180 (S1L-g's `<style> package { MinimumWidth }` consumer) 0 -> 3.038715 before the floor was threaded back in. The package-folder-tab bucket is now EMPTY: its last two fixtures were misattributions the heuristic made on a leading `artifact`/`package` keyword, both re-bucketed in CAUSE_PATTERNS -- codabo-50-mupa164 is CREOLE TITLED SEPARATORS (`--title1--`/`==title2==` draw a rule carrying their title text, so they contribute the TITLE's width 37.6px, not the raw markup's 62.5px; every other node in that fixture is exact) and tajadu-40-juro990 is a MULTI-LINE QUOTED DISPLAY (upstream's CommandCreateElementMultilines joins the continuation lines; we stop at the first, leaving the id literally `foo2 as \"This artifact` -- its other three nodes are exact). S1L-d (2026-07-28) wired `skinparam wrapWidth` into the SIZER. Fission (the Neutron word-wrap) was ALREADY ported and ALREADY used by the leaf RENDERER (EntityImageDescriptionSupport.ts#buildWrappedLines); leaf-sizing.ts simply never called it, so a wrapped diagram measured its boxes at the unwrapped single-line width while the renderer drew them wrapped -- the same sizer<->renderer divergence family as creole-lexer-unification. New leaf-sizing-text.ts#measureTextBlock reuses getSplitted (never re-derives the break positions), threaded via ClassifyCtx.wrapWidth -> BoxSizingOpts.wrapWidth; maxWidth 0 (upstream's own default -- it sets PName.MaximumWidth nowhere) delegates to the unwrapped helpers unchanged, so this is zero-diff for every diagram that does not set the skinparam. Wiring it made mejoxi-96-cegu294's HEIGHTS exact immediately (58/72) with widths still 4.9875 short, which isolated a SECOND, independent bug in the same fixture: the `[\"...\"]` bracket shorthand was stripping quotes that upstream KEEPS. Upstream's eventuallyRemoveStartingAndEndingDoubleQuote (java:311) sees the display with its brackets still attached, so it no-ops and the bracket wrapper comes off afterwards -- our parseBracketDeclaration passed the ALREADY unbracketed body through stripFullWrap. Jar-verified: `[plain]` draws plain, `[\"quoted\"]` draws \"quoted\", while `component \"cq\"` and `component cq2 as \"dq\"` do strip. (The 4.9875 was one `\"` glyph; unwrapped the gap was exactly twice that, both quotes on one line.) mejoxi-96 now exact at 238.100x58 / 238.362x72. 279 -> 280/351 (79.5 -> 79.8 pct), zero widened; the wrapWidth bucket is EMPTY. S1L-f part 2a (2026-07-28), four fixes that each unmasked the next. (1) SPRITE SCALE: `CommandCreoleSprite.java:82` scales a creole `<$name>` by `Parser.getScale(...) * fc.getSize2D() / 13.0` -- the requested scale TIMES the ambient font size over a 13px reference -- and it applies to EVERY sprite kind, since the factor lives in the creole command, not in any Sprite class. This port used the raw registry dims * requested scale, i.e. silently assumed font 13. Jar-verified at two sizes and two kinds: a 48x48 encoded sprite measures 51.6923 at font 14 and 96.0 at font 26; a 16x16 SVG sprite 17.2308 and 32.0. New `spriteScale` in creole-atoms-measure.ts (creole-atoms.ts was split at the 500-line cap); both RENDER sites now thread their own font so drawn and measured sprite geometry cannot drift. (2) PER-ATOM FONTS: the sizer concatenated every text atom and measured the result at the BASE font, which is exact only while every atom shares that size -- wrong for a `==heading` line (`fontConfigurationForHeading`: order 0 -> +4, 1 -> +2, 2 -> +1) or a `<size:N>` run. `buildLineAtoms` already returns atoms under their own cascaded fonts (the renderer's `measureAtomsWidthHeight` had always summed per-atom), so `lineTextMetrics` now does the same. (3) STEREOTYPE IN A QUOTED DISPLAY: `parseNameSection` rejoined the quoted display before scanning for decoration, so guillemets INSIDE the quotes were extracted as a stereotype AND left in the display -- reserving one extra stereotype line (+lineH) plus STEREO_MARGIN (+2). Upstream's STEREOTYPE group sits after the CODE/DISPLAY alternatives, so it can only match after the closing quote. (4) GUILLEMET: `CreoleParser.java:175` runs `skinParam.guillemet().manageGuillemet(line)` before stripes are built, so `<<x>>` in DISPLAY text draws as the two glyphs `\u00abx\u00bb`, not four literal chars -- 17.3px too wide per occurrence here. Ported to core/text/Guillemet.ts and threaded through BOTH the sizer (ClassifyCtx -> BoxSizingOpts) and the renderer (buildTextBlock), honouring `skinparam guillemet` (mogidu-85-roxe269 sets `none`). Net: 280 -> 284/351 (79.8 -> 80.9 pct), zero widened. nenedo-78-fiva569 drove all four: 6 of its 8 nodes are now exact. Class ratchet unmoved (219/708, zero widened); class/component/usecase structure 708/262/90 all still 100 pct EQUAL. Five unit expectations that had encoded the missing /13 (and one toBe->toBeCloseTo for per-atom summation's ~1e-14 association drift) were corrected. STILL OPEN for S1L-f part 2b: SVG-form sprites (`sprite N <svg ...>`) are not parsed at all -- bootstrap AND archimate are both SVG-sprite bundles, so ruziru-69/bootstrap-0/tatori-66/sprite-SVG-fill-management-3/turasu-73 still measure their sprites as 0. S1L-f part 2b (2026-07-28) ported SVG-form sprites. `sprite N <svg ...>` (CommandSpriteSvg, single-line) and its multi-line form (CommandSpriteSvgMultiline, END = a line ending `</svg>`) were not in the grammar at all -- only the encoded `[WxH/Nz]` forms were -- so bootstrap AND archimate, which are BOTH SVG-sprite bundles, registered nothing and every `<$name>` from them measured 0. New core/klimt/sprite/SpriteSvg.ts carries `UImageSvg#getData`'s dimension rule exactly: a viewBox WINS outright (width = its 3rd number, height its 4th, each Math.ceil'd), else the `width=`/`height=` attribute inside the `<svg ...>` tag read as leading digits. That precedence is why archimate's `width=\"19.995mm\"` never needs unit handling -- its viewBox supplies the number. getSpriteMonochrome now DECLINES an SVG sprite (it was an unchecked cast) and render-atoms.ts re-emits the element as an image/svg+xml data URI, untinted (upstream's SpriteSvg ignores fontColor/forcedColor too). descriptive-keywords.ts strips SVG sprite regions from the dispatch scan window as well -- bootstrap is ~7200 lines of them, the same burial that made stripSpriteRegions necessary for the encoded form. Also closed the gap measureUsecase's own doc comment had flagged (\"no corpus fixture exercises a tall atom inside a use-case label\"): the ellipse footprint now includes atomHeightBonus on the HEIGHT axis, not just the width. 284 -> 286/351 (80.9 -> 81.5 pct), zero widened; tatori-66-kaci883 + sprite-SVG-fill-management-3 (the two inline-SVG fixtures) are CONFORMANT. leaf-sizing.ts was split again at the 500-line cap into leaf-sizing-consts.ts + leaf-sizing-folder.ts. OPEN, precisely characterised: ruziru-69-xixo434/bootstrap-0 still miss because a sprite's USE-CASE footprint is not always its box. Jar-measured: `bi-globe` at scale 2.5 measures 43.077 inside a RECTANGLE but only 39.642 inside a USECASE, while `bi-bootstrap-fill` measures 43.077 in BOTH -- same declared `<svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\">`, same scale, both syntaxes (`,scale=` and `{scale=}`) agreeing. So the ellipse path uses something CONTENT-dependent, most likely SvgNanoParser's drawn-ink bounds rather than the declared box. Porting that is an SVG path-bbox subsystem -- its own mission, NOT a divergence.",
